  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S R K Products Company vs The Union Of India on 22 March, 2024 Author: Surepalli Nanda Bench: Surepalli Nanda Hon'Ble Mrs Justice Surepalli Nanda Writ Petition No.13208 of 2013 Order: The copy of the Judgment is enclosed herewith.\" M/S R K Products Company vs The Union Of India on 22 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/18386769/ 1",
    "facts": "6. A criminal case was filed by Sub Inspector/Government Railway Police, Secunderabad, a separate wing controlled by the State Authority and the case was filed before concerned Hon'ble Magistrate and numbered as CC No.895/2013 against the owner of the seized Gutka and not the Writ Petitioner. The Accused/Owner of seized goods pleaded guilty and was convicted by the Hon'ble II Metropolitan Magistrate for Railways, Secunderabad vide Judgment dt. 26-9-2013.",
    "arguments": "2. The petitioner approached the Court seeking prayer as under: \"...to issue a direction or a writ one in the nature of Writ of Mandamus declaring the action of the respondent in Seizing the consignment containing Sagar Gutka packets under the joint Survey proceedings dt 11-03-2013 as illegal contrary to law and judicial precedents and consequently direct the respondent to release the same and be pleased pass orders as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit.\" 3. The learned counsel appearing on behalf of respondents has filed counter affidavit and in particular, paragraph Nos. 4, 5 and 6 of the said counter affidavit reads as under: \"4. As per the Joint Survey only 80 bags of prohibited pan masala for loading by Train A.P. Express to be transported to Jammu were seized and not as falsely contended by the Petitioner in Para 3 and ground no.1 of the Affidavit. 5."
  },
